      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rutledge%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1801 Rutledge became Grainger County's first town with its own police department.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rutledge%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits in Richland Valley, a 35‑mile stretch along Clinch Mountain between Blaine and Bean Station.",
